Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/PlaqueBoyMax.md` and appended the fresh-eyes notes at the bottom (no body edits). This also fills in the pipeline's fresh-eyes stage, which last night's 2 AM run left as an empty log.

The two biggest issues I flagged:

1. **The trophy ledger hides the losses that prove its own thesis.** He lost Streamer of the Year to IShowSpeed in December 2025 — the one nomination that was purely his name — and "Victory Lap" lost its Grammy category at the February 2026 ceremony. The draft goes from "Grammy nomination" straight to "Brit Award win" and never says how Grammy night ended, which reads as protective. A loss row would make "the one column he can't fill" land harder.

2. **The Streamer University aftermath is vaguer than the record.** "Creators lined up publicly to defend him" skips the concrete beat: roommate WardrobeWinter stood up for him and they won Best Roommates at the SU awards — which is also the best live evidence for the Rabbit Hole's stress/security loyalty claim. And the section closes too neatly given that OjaySuave has since publicly alleged Max had them removed from the show; the story is still moving.

Smaller notes in the block: the naming scene and the 30-slide deck are each told one-to-two times too many (the ending re-narrates the cold open), the seven-figure gambling refusal is buried in the skippable Rabbit Hole when it's the strongest "what he won't do for a number" beat, and the aunt ($2k clean-graduation deal → chief of staff) is a through-line currently split across body and Rabbit Hole. I also marked the ledger table, the hollow million-follower interior beat, and the wigs-as-inventory paragraph as the spine to preserve.

